# Hand-written text that already carries a FULL DATE the family tree attaches to a person the
# living rule (kit living_rule.py, 16 October 2026) calls living, found the first time
# tools/livingcheck.py looked with the GEDCOM beside it. Eight files, in two groups:
#
#   A. a state birth-register extract, transcribed in full: a birth date (with a hospital and a time)
#      of a person born in 1951. /certificate/ is the transcription; /sources/ and
#      site/src/data/sources.json quote it; photos/hedviga/index.md is the photograph note that
#      first transcribed it; README.md names the same extract by its issue date, which is the same
#      day, so the date there is Hedviga's certificate and not the birth, and is listed because the
#      gate cannot tell the two apart.
#   B. a correction that quotes a tree entry's BIRTH DATE for a woman born in 1960 to show that an
#      attachment does not hold: /people/marica-milkovic/, /corrections/ and
#      site/src/data/corrections.json.
#
# THIS FILE NAMES THE FILE AND HOW MANY. It never records the date or the person: a list of living
# people's dates is exactly what must not be committed. A file listed here may carry up to that many;
# one more fails the build (tools/livingcheck.py, rules GED-DATE and GED-YEAR).
#
# These are research prose and were NOT rewritten (David, 16 October 2026): each is somebody's
# decision, either the date comes off the page or the page stands as the research record. Removing
# a row here is the goal; adding one needs a reason.
#
# file or page|count|kind|why
certificate|1|birth date, hospital and time (transcribed state extract)|group A
sources|1|birth date (quotes the extract)|group A
site/src/data/sources.json|1|birth date (quotes the extract)|group A, the data behind /sources/
photos/hedviga/index.md|1|birth date, hospital and time (photograph note)|group A, a research note
README.md|1|issue date of the extract, which is also the birth date|group A, coincidence the gate cannot tell apart
people/marica-milkovic|1|birth date (quoted from a tree entry in a correction)|group B
corrections|1|birth date (quoted from a tree entry in a correction)|group B
site/src/data/corrections.json|2|birth date, and the birth year on two lines (quoted from a tree entry in a correction)|group B, the data behind /corrections/ and the person page
